{"id":"late-or-missing-statements","title":"Board and commission members who filed the yearly statement late, or not at all","question":"How many members of boards and commissions filed their yearly statement of economic interests after the deadline while holding a seat, on which bodies, and what followed?","finding":"Of 2,134 yearly statements filed by board and commission members for 2021 to 2025, 124 (6%) were filed after April 10 of the following year, when the first list of non-filers is drawn up. The Ethics Commission's own count for all filers in 2025 is 337 late (5.7%) and 79 not filed (1.3%) of 5,958, and its list of June 2, 2025 still showed 6 board members and commissioners without a Form 700; it opened cases on 21 of 234 people still out of compliance after a grace period. 13 penalties on record are for not filing the form, $33,945 in all.","how":"Cover pages of yearly (annual) Form 700 statements filed by people holding a seat as commissioner, board member, trustee, director or committee member, for calendar years 2021 to 2025, the years in which every filer files electronically. The first yearly statement each person filed for a year is compared with April 10 of the following year. Bodies with fewer than ten statements are not listed. The citywide figures are quoted from the Ethics Commission's December 2025 enforcement report and its list of officers and employees without 2025 filings; penalties are from its penalty file. The older non-filer lists (2015 to 2021, 269 rows) are tabulated in the “interests” results and not repeated.","limits":"Late is not never: almost everyone on the lists files within weeks, and a member appointed in mid-year files on a different schedule. The exact deadline moves by a day or two when April 1 falls on a weekend, which is why April 10 is used; a statement filed on April 2 is not counted late here. This file holds statements that were filed, so a member who never filed at all appears only on the Commission's lists, which are published as web pages for the current year and not kept as data after 2021. A member who has left the body by the time the list is drawn may still be shown on it.","tier":"OFFICIAL","columns":[{"k":"body","t":"Board or commission","type":"text"},{"k":"members","t":"Members filing","type":"int"},{"k":"statements","t":"Yearly statements, 2021 to 2025","type":"int"},{"k":"late","t":"Filed after April 10","type":"int"},{"k":"lateShare","t":"Share late","type":"pct"},{"k":"late60","t":"More than 60 days after","type":"int"},{"k":"repeat","t":"Members late in two or more years","type":"int"},{"k":"worstDays","t":"Longest delay","type":"days"}],"rows":[{"body":"Planning Commission","members":14,"statements":37,"late":8,"lateShare":0.216,"late60":6,"repeat":2,"worstDays":1333},{"body":"Treasure Island Development Authority","members":8,"statements":28,"late":6,"lateShare":0.214,"late60":3,"repeat":1,"worstDays":1069},{"body":"Revenue Bond Oversight Committee","members":5,"statements":14,"late":3,"lateShare":0.214,"late60":1,"repeat":1,"worstDays":400},{"body":"Commission on the Status of Women","members":10,"statements":32,"late":6,"lateShare":0.188,"late60":3,"repeat":1,"worstDays":1087},{"body":"Board of Examiners","members":15,"statements":47,"late":7,"lateShare":0.149,"late60":4,"repeat":1,"worstDays":985},{"body":"Redevelopment Successor Agency Oversight Board","members":6,"statements":25,"late":3,"lateShare":0.12,"late60":3,"repeat":1,"worstDays":1075},{"body":"Homelessness Oversight Commission","members":7,"statements":17,"late":2,"lateShare":0.118,"late60":2,"repeat":1,"worstDays":587},{"body":"Refuse Rate Board","members":3,"statements":10,"late":1,"lateShare":0.1,"late60":1,"repeat":null,"worstDays":195},{"body":"Citizens General Obligation Bond Oversight Committee","members":12,"statements":31,"late":3,"lateShare":0.097,"late60":1,"repeat":null,"worstDays":484},{"body":"Human Services Commission","members":5,"statements":21,"late":2,"lateShare":0.095,"late6